[h1]NM - Energy Tab[/h1]
Your colony's power system in one tab. Compare generation and consumption, find unpowered devices, and keep track of battery reserves.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/neuromanser89/neuromanser-workshop-assets/main/shared/sections/en/description-v1.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Map overview and individual networks.[/b] Generation, actual consumption, balance and battery charge for the current map or selected network. Show network moves the camera to its buildings and selects them.
[*][b]Visible problems.[/b] Counters for no power, breakdowns, disconnected devices and EMP open the matching devices.
[*][b]Consumers and generators.[/b] Search, sorting, state filters, device counts and power shares. Open a group to inspect individual buildings and locate them on the map.
[*][b]Power and charge history.[/b] Charts for 5, 15 or 60 minutes, highlighted deficits and values on hover.
[*][b]Discharge forecast.[/b] Select a connected network to estimate remaining battery time in game hours at the current load.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/neuromanser89/neuromanser-workshop-assets/main/mods/neuro-energy/en/screenshots/v1/01-consumers.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/neuromanser89/neuromanser-workshop-assets/main/shared/sections/en/compatibility-v1.png[/img]
[b]RimWorld 1.6.[/b] No DLC, Harmony or other mods required. English and Russian interface. The mod displays data and does not change electricity mechanics.

Includes player-owned buildings on the current map using the standard power system. Custom energy systems from other mods may not appear. A positive map balance does not guarantee power in every separate network.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/neuromanser89/neuromanser-workshop-assets/main/shared/sections/en/faq-v1.png[/img]
[b]What do the chart minutes mean?[/b]
Real time excluding pauses. A snapshot is taken every 5 seconds; game speed does not change this interval.

[b]Is history saved?[/b]
The last 60 minutes of map history are saved with the colony. Individual network history is collected during the current session and resets when network membership changes; it starts over after loading.

[b]How accurate is the battery forecast?[/b]
It is an estimate at current consumption and generation, excluding self-discharge and charging losses. Weather and devices switching on change the estimate. Disconnected batteries count toward map inventory, but not a connected network's forecast.

[b]Can I add or remove it in an existing save?[/b]
The mod adds no items or research, but adding and removing it in existing saves has not yet been separately tested.

